  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REECALL 2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project scopes include local government, local authorities at union, Upazila, district and national level, market actor, think tank organization and other relevant stakeholders for the sustainable and functional relation for developing community resilience to social economical and climate induced calamities. Through Bangladesh Rural Resilience actions, we will reach 1,00,000 direct project participants and of them 60% are women, 30% are youth and 10% are men. During the outline duration, emphasis will be given to showcasing and advocating resilience best practices with wide range of stakeholders including donor communities and affiliates and governments. On the other hand, youth groups will be Linked with National Youth Council to access skills training, employability, and leaderships. Producer groups and small scale Income Generating Activity (IGA), Enterprises will be linked with prospective economic opportunities, production marketing and management skills. Community Based Organisations (CBOs) will work further with Disabled Persons Organizations (DPOs) and capacitate them to claim their rights and disabled friendly economic opportunities. Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) Initiatives and infrastructures will be handed over formally to local government and Department of Public Health Engineering (DPHE) with increasing further engagement of Women WASH platforms. Oxfam in Bangladesh along with 14 national and local implementing Partners will collectively conduct research, study, impact evaluation, gender audit and organize learning sharing events at different level from local to national. In addition, 14 Partners with support from Oxfam in Bangladesh will roll out exit plan and strategies with communities, local government, line departments, Civil Society Organisations (CSOs). Side by side, concepts/proposals will shape up further taking resilience journey implementation aspirations through sense making Events, Partner Non Government Organisations (PNGOs) cap</narrative>
  </description>
